<title>GERMANY: AMB seeks merger with AM Konzernrueck.</title>
<headline>AMB seeks merger with AM Konzernrueck.</headline>
<dateline>AACHEN, Germany 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>German insurance group AMB Aachener und Muenchener Beteligungs AG said on Friday it planned to merge with reinsurer AM Konzernrueckversicherungs AG, of which it owns 90.8 percent.</p>
<p>In a joint statement, the two companies said a merger would allow them to establish a co-ordinated reinsurance strategy to the benefit of all companies in the AMB group.</p>
<p>Although valuations were not yet complete, the statement said that the value per share of AM Konzernrueckversicherungs AG was expected to be higher than its current traded value.</p>
<p>A final decision on the merger had not yet been taken.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
